Executive Director
Organization: Legal Aid Services of Oregon (LASO)
Location: Portland, OR
Date Posted: 09/14/2026
Executive Director
Legal Aid Services of Oregon (LASO)
seeks an Executive Director to lead this civil legal aid organization as it begins its next chapter. The organization has a staff of 101 (including 56 attorneys), eight regional offices, four statewide programs and an annual budget of approximately $13 million. This is an exciting opportunity for a strong leader with vision and creativity to build on LASO’s proud 52-year history and to expand and strengthen access to justice, empower communities, and facilitate systemic change in Oregon.
Background
LASO is a not-for-profit organization that represents low-income clients in civil cases. LASO’s eight regional offices serve the general low-income population throughout Oregon and four specialized statewide programs provide services to farmworkers, taxpayers with tax controversies, the Native American community, and those needing pro bono referrals to the private bar. LASO is an effective, high-quality legal services program committed to advocacy strategies with the broadest possible impact on client community problems. LASO is actively working to build an inclusive organizational culture that recognizes the value of racial equity. LASO is committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse workforce and providing a welcoming and culturally responsive environment for staff and clients.
LASO, an LSC funded program, works cooperatively with its sister organization, the Oregon Law Center (OLC). Together, they have a long history of providing critical legal services and act as a community resource to resolve some of the most pressing challenges facing low-income Oregon residents.
LASO’s central administrative offices are based in Portland, Oregon, and its executive team engages with all its offices across the state. LASO provides legal services that are vitally important to its clients. LASO’s legal work encompasses, among other things, family law, housing, public benefits, elder law, and employment law. In addition to providing individual legal representation and counseling for clients, LASO does broad impact work that benefits low-income individuals through advocacy, legal self-help materials, community outreach and education, and working with coalitions to pursue common goals. LASO, working with OLC, has been a leader in the state in recognizing and addressing systemic problems affecting low-income residents.
Why Legal Aid Services of Oregon?
LASO has an excellent reputation and strong network of partnerships and connections throughout the region with a track record of innovation and responsiveness to community needs. The Executive Director will work with experienced LASO staff and management, a committed Board of Directors, and supportive community advocates, private lawyers, government agencies and donors.
LASO provides a diverse range of vital services to more than 4,500 clients annually. An estimated 615,230 people are eligible for legal services in LASO’s footprint.
Why Oregon?
Oregon features diverse and beautiful landscapes that include the Oregon Coast, the Cascade Mountains and Columbia River Gorge which provide the venues for unequalled outdoor recreation opportunities including hiking, backpacking, biking, skiing, fishing, and windsurfing. Oregon’s Willamette Valley is home to numerous wineries and is known for producing some of the world’s best Chardonnay. The Willamette Valley is also the most agriculturally diverse region in Oregon producing over 170 different crops and is the nation’s largest producer of hazelnuts and cranberries and one of the largest producers of Christmas trees and grass seed. Nike and Intel are its most well-known corporations. The University of Oregon, Oregon State University, Willamette University, Lewis and Clark College, and Reed College are the state’s major universities and colleges.
Why Portland?
Portland is home to Powell’s Books City of Books, the largest independent bookstore in the world that takes up a city block and has over a million titles. Portland’s city limits are also home to the 5,200-acre Forest Park, which has 80 miles of hiking trails, and Washington Park, a 410-acre park that boasts a Japanese Garden universally considered the finest example of a Japanese Garden outside of Japan. Downtown Portland’s Saturday Market is the largest continually operated outdoor market in the US. Portland is considered one of the highest-ranking restaurant towns in the United States, with restaurants regularly rated among the best in North America. The restaurant scene in Portland also includes over 500 food carts that are part of a vibrant neighborhood culture. Portland’s unofficial motto is “Keep Portland Weird.”
High-Priority Roles and Responsibilities for the Next Executive Director
Serve as an effective ambassador for the organization, nurturing collaborative relationships with client communities, community partners, funders and grantors, elected officials, private bar and judicial leaders, private donors, and business and civic organizations throughout the state;
Working to expand LASO’s corporate and foundation support and, working with Oregon’s Campaign for Equal Justice, expand the financial support necessary to carry out the organization’s activities, including from Oregon’s legal community and individual donors;
Support and foster a culture that builds a sense of a statewide program with a shared mission and consistent policies, promotes mutual respect and teamwork and an environment in which staff are valued, supported and committed to the mission and work;
Work with the Oregon Law Center to coordinate services in order to maximize the impact on the client communities the organizations serve;
Maintain a collaborative relationship with other legal aid organizations and other antipoverty organizations in Oregon;
Provide leadership and nurture the values of LASO, including access to justice, a holistic view of client services, ease of access for new clients, prioritization of strategies that address the causes of legal problems and management of staff relations;
Provide regular communications to staff and Board, facilitate Board operations and provide fiscal oversight to the organization; and
Implement the strategic plan for LASO.
Desired Qualifications and Experience of the Successful Candidate
Exhibit excellent communication skills and the ability to build relationships with and to inspire the trust and confidence of LASO staff, Board members, client communities, community partners, donors, funders, and other stakeholders and allies, including the will and ability to engage in difficult conversations as circumstances may dictate;
Have fundraising and/or grant writing knowledge and/or experience;
Have the ability to think strategically and creatively;
Possess demonstrated and exceptional leadership in managing and supervising a successful legal services organization, law firm, corporate law department, branch of a court system, relevant government agency or not-for-profit organization;
Demonstrate knowledge of the laws and issues affecting low-income people and a passion for social, economic, and racial justice;
Have experience in building a team environment, including working with a labor union and collective bargaining agreement, to encourage professional development of staff, and supporting staff in the program’s work;
Have experience working with organizations and individuals with a variety of perspectives, including clients, staff, Board members, the public, and elected and appointed officials;
Possess personal attributes including professionalism, integrity, the ability to engender confidence and trust, honesty, a strong work ethic, a sense of humor, empathy, courage, a collaborative spirit, and an openness to diverse voices;
Understand financial matters, including development of budgets, compliance with grant and contract requirements, union negotiations, and financial oversight;
Be skilled at managing and allocating limited resources appropriately;
Be a licensed attorney, in good standing, with the expectation that the successful candidate will be admitted, or able to be admitted, to the Oregon Bar in a reasonable period of time;
Have at least ten years of legal experience as a lawyer or as a manager in the not-for-profit sector, preferably in the public interest sector, and/or with previous legal aid experience.
Location
This is primarily an on-site position at the Portland office. Periodic travel throughout the state is required.
Salary
Projected range of $140,000 to $160,000 D.O.E. Excellent fringe benefits.
Application Process
Legal Aid Services of Oregon is assisted in its search by: Dennis Groenenboom, Consultant.
Materials should be submitted electronically to
[email protected]
in Microsoft Word or PDF format. Candidates with questions about the position or process are encouraged to contact Dennis at the email address above or at 515-537-4242.
Screening of applicants begins immediately and will continue until the time of selection. To receive full consideration, you should submit your application materials by
October 1, 2026
. To apply, submit a letter expressing your interest in the position, your qualifications for the job, bar status, and what you believe you will be able to contribute to enhance the ability of LASO to provide high-quality, client focused services into the future. Please also include a description of your personal efforts, personal or otherwise, to promote Diversity, Equity and Inclusion and the results of those efforts. Please include a resume/CV and the names and contact information for three professional references.
If you require reasonable accommodation for a disability during the application/hiring process, please contact
[email protected]
.
LASO celebrates diversity. LASO is committed to being an organization that reflects the communities served and is diverse i

Senior Managing Director, Global Performance Marketing and Media
Organization: Humane World for Animals
Location: Remote
Date Posted: 10/05/2026
The general salary range for this full-time position is $115,000 – 185,000. Salary offers will be commensurate with experience, qualifications, skills, training and education.
Humane World for Animals, a global leader in animal advocacy and protection, is seeking a Senior Managing Director, Global Performance Marketing and Media for the Global Marketing Performance and Media department. In this position you will lead the organizations’ paid media team, responsible for establishing and scaling our customer acquisition strategy and day-to-day management and directing of the performance channels to reach organizational advocacy, branding, fundraising, and list growth goals.
Responsibilities:
Lead the development, execution and analysis of the organization’s paid media and performance marketing programs using a portfolio of paid channels including search, display, social media, DRTV, CTV, Podcasts and third-party list buys; manage budget in excess of $13 million and drive 40K new donors, 11K sustainers and $4MM in first year revenue. Identify goals and develop comprehensive marketing plans to execute large-scale, segmented donor acquisition and retention programs by partnering with external vendors and internal fundraising teams. Collaborate across multiple business functions including Brand Marketing, Digital Marketing, Acquisition Marketing, Philanthropy, Data Analytics, Campaigns and Finance to measure impact of brand and performance media on organization’s overall fundraising, advocacy and brand strategy;
Direct planning, execution and reporting on performance of paid advertising and third-party acquisition partners. Direct the development of blended attribution models to fully realize effect of advertising spend;
Set strategic vision for a multi-year strategy that accelerates supporter growth and retention. Lead budget planning and management for paid digital, TV and audio program. Create and execute multi-year planning strategies to support long-term revenue and retention goals, as well as brand positioning objectives. Identify integration opportunities and ensure campaign efforts deliver consistent, engaging experiences throughout the acquisition funnel; oversee regular testing of donation funnel, adjusting strategy based on response rates;
Elevate organizations global social media program to support advocacy, community, brand and fundraising objectives across over 100 social media handles throughout the globe;
Lead global test and invest efforts across the organization to identify and evaluate new media and partner opportunities to ensure marketing strategy remains leading edge, including the integration of evolving marketing technologies and capabilities;
Evaluate and monitor performance of brand media campaigns in partnership with the brand team and third party partners;
Lead initiatives to understand, segment and target priority audiences for both prospecting (acquisition) and retention;
Provide leadership, organizational development, and management for a growing team;
Performs other duties as assigned.
Qualifications and Requirements:
Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, design, journalism, English, liberal arts, communications or other relevant field, or equivalent work experience required. MBA preferred;
A minimum of ten (10) years of experience in digital marketing and media acquisition required;
Management experience in a related field, which has included management and leadership responsibilities for staff, strategy development and execution, and fiscal and budget accountabilities, preferably in the animal welfare arena required;
Experience applying analytical thinking, leveraging both quantitative and qualitative data to identify, prioritize and pursue opportunities required;
Experience with TV, Radio, Streaming, Google AdWords, Facebook Business Manager, and Google Analytics desired;
Demonstrated strong leadership, communication and collaboration skills directing multiple projects and leading cross-functional initiatives to meet business goals; ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects simultaneously;
Ability to communicate a strategic vision for team of channel leaders with clearly defined strategies, KPIs and goals;
Demonstrated, intensive knowledge of broadcast media, the Internet, online trends, and the use of the Internet for fundraising and/or social change, and familiarity with social media and paid advertising techniques;
Advanced knowledge of advertising creative development, including an understanding of how consumers engage with direct-response media and the levers that drive performance;
Demonstrated ability to compile, analyze and leverage performance data to both identify new opportunities and optimize existing campaigns;
Excellent written and verbal communication and presentation skills essential;
Strong decision-making, organizational, planning, and complex problem-solving skills essential;
Demonstrated ability to manage multiple, competing priorities, duties, and projects desired;
Positive, collaborate mindset with interest in testing and exploring new, innovative solutions;
Leadership ability in work setting. Flexible, willing to learn, and anticipates the needs of self and staff;
Ability to set a positive tone for employees during their day. Strong coach and delegator to team members;
Comfortable in a fast-paced environment with frequent deadlines; high energy, self-motivated and proactive;
Ability to manage issues requiring problem resolution and conflict management with excellent interpersonal and intervention skills;
Strong knowledge of business operations, including effective budget development and management processes;
Strong attention to detail and commitment to excellence, demonstrated by the delivery of quality and timely outcomes;
Strong interest in animal protection issues preferred.
This is a full-time remote position based in the United States. Candidates must be able to accommodate Eastern Time hours, as needed.
Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, and disability, marital or parental status or protected veteran status. EOE
